    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nDNG Phibsboro are delighted to present to the market 3 Burnside Lane, a stylish and well presented two bedroom, two bathroom mid terrace home. Modernised throughout, the property combines contemporary finishes with generous living accommodation and a particularly attractive south facing rear garden. The property is ideally suited to those seeking a modern home in a convenient and well established location.\n\nUpon entering, the property opens into a contemporary kitchen/dining room featuring modern fitted cabinetry and updated appliances, creating a bright and practical space for everyday dining. A dedicated breakfast nook provides an additional area for casual dining, while the modern finishes throughout give the room a sleek and contemporary feel. To the rear is a light filled living room, offering a generous and comfortable space with a feature fireplace creating an attractive focal point. Sliding doors provide direct access to the south facing rear garden, allowing excellent natural light into the room and creating a seamless connection between the indoor and outdoor spaces. The living room is further complemented by attractive ceiling coving, adding character to the contemporary interior. A separate utility room is located to the rear, providing useful additional storage and practical space.\n\nUpstairs are two generously sized double bedrooms. The main bedroom benefits from its own ensuite bathroom, while a separate family bathroom is conveniently positioned on the landing. Both bedrooms offer excellent proportions and ample space for bedroom furniture.\n\nBurnside Lane is situated in a convenient and well established residential location, with a wide range of local amenities, shops, cafés and recreational facilities available nearby. The property is well positioned for access to Dublin City Centre, with regular bus services operating in the surrounding area. The M50 and M1 are also readily accessible, providing convenient connectivity to Dublin Airport and the wider Dublin road network. The location also offers easy access to a number of established employment, educational and recreational facilities, making it an attractive option for both owner occupiers and investors.\n\nPlease Note: Some images have been digitally staged using AI to illustrate the potential of the property and its furnishings. These are for illustrative purposes only."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nEntrance Hall - 3.93m x 1.72m\nA welcoming entrance hall with attractive sleek flooring extending throughout, creating a bright and contemporary first impression. The hallway provides access to all ground floor accommodation, with the kitchen/dining room positioned immediately to the right upon entering.\n\nKitchen/Dining Room - 3.69m x 1.91m\nThe kitchen/dining room is a particularly impressive space, featuring modern fitted cabinetry and a range of updated appliances. The contemporary finishes are complemented by tiled flooring, while a dedicated breakfast nook provides an excellent additional area for casual dining. The room offers a practical and stylish setting for everyday living and entertaining, with generous natural light adding to its appeal.\n\nLiving Room - 4.94m x 3.73m\nTo the rear of the property is a bright and generously proportioned living room, finished with attractive flooring and centred around a feature fireplace which provides a charming focal point. Sliding doors open directly onto the south facing rear garden, creating an excellent connection between the living accommodation and outdoor space while allowing an abundance of natural light into the room. Attractive ceiling coving adds a further touch of character, while useful storage is also incorporated within the room\n\nUtilitly Room - \nThe separate utility room is conveniently positioned to the rear of the property and provides excellent practical functionality. Efficiently laid out and plumbed for a washing machine, the room also houses the boiler and provides useful additional storage, helping to keep the main living accommodation uncluttered\n\nBedroom 1 - 3.13m x 3.62m\nLocated to the rear of the property, the main bedroom is a spacious double room featuring carpet flooring and fitted wardrobes, providing excellent built in storage. The room enjoys a pleasant outlook over the south-facing rear garden and benefits from excellent proportions, comfortably accommodating a range of bedroom furniture. A private ensuite bathroom further complements this well-appointed bedroom.\n\nBedroom 2 - 2.81m x 3.62m\nPositioned to the front of the property, the second bedroom is another generously sized double room, finished with carpet flooring and complemented by fitted wardrobes. The room enjoys a pleasant outlook over the front green area and provides ample space for bedroom furniture, making it an ideal second bedroom, guest room or home office.\n\nEnsuite Bathroom - 1.74m x 0.75m\nThe ensuite is fully tiled and comprises a WC, wash hand basin and shower unit. A heated towel rail and contemporary finishes complete this practical and well-presented space.\n\nFamily Bathroom - 1.49m x 1.69m\nThe family bathroom is conveniently located on the first floor landing and is fully tiled throughout. The accommodation comprises a bath with shower unit, WC and wash hand basin, with the tiled finish providing a clean and contemporary appearance.\n\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li> 2 Bed, 2 Bath Mid-terrace home</li><li> BER: C1</li><li> Approx 66 SQ.M</li><li> Gas fired central heating</li><li> Gated complex</li><li> Management fee: 750.00</li><li> Excellent access to Dublin City Centre with regular bus services nearby, while the M1 and M50 are readily accessible, providing convenient links to Dublin Airport and the wider road network.</li><li> Set in a well-established residential area close to a wide range of local shops, cafés, amenities and recreational facilities, with easy access to established employment and educational centres</ul>"
      },
